        ":question/id": "f8f45df0-069c-5e4a-a4d7-bdd2e15f5467",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-86429",
        ":question/problem": "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=6{x}^{2}+2y$ at the point $(0,1)$ in the direction of the vector $v=3i+5j.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{\u2032}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{\u2032}(a,b)=\u2207f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016v\u2016 & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{5}^{2}}=\\sqrt{34} \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{34}}(3i+5j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $\u2207f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\,f(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(6{x}^{2}+2y)\\text{\u00a0}i+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(6{x}^{2}+2y)\\text{\u00a0}j \\\\  & =12x\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ \u2207\\,f(0,1) & =(12\\cdot 0)\\,i+2\\,j \\\\  & =2j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{\u2032}(0,1) & =\u2207\\,f(0,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =2j\\cdot (\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{34}}i+\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{34}}j) \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 5}{\\sqrt{34}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\sqrt{34}}{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
